From 4ff0781ae21bb778bff076aaacb53dfac339c2dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:57:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] media: iris: support decode-order output on HFI gen2

Clients using synchronous per-picture decoding, such as VA-API users,
can wait for a decoded picture before submitting further input. Firmware
returning pictures in display order can withhold that picture until later
input arrives, preventing such clients from making progress.

Expose the standard decoder display-delay controls through the HFI gen2
decoder capability table. Support only a zero display delay, which maps
to decode-order output, and leave the feature disabled by default. Use
the existing control handling to reject changes while OUTPUT is streaming.

Set HFI_PROP_DECODE_ORDER_OUTPUT through the decoder input configuration
path before starting OUTPUT. Leave the firmware default untouched until
userspace sets the enable control, and send its value on subsequent
starts so disabling the control restores display-order output in the
same session. Propagate failures through the configuration path.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
